{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543429-m20-story-wise-questions-about-the-magick-system","id":1543429,"title":"[M20] Story-wise questions about the magick system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-09T09:43:07-07:00","id":1543429,"title":"[M20] Story-wise questions about the magick system","content":"About to run my first M20 session, and while I understand how magick and casting Effects work mechanically, I do have some questions about casting magick, primarily with character's foci.<br /> <br /> 1. How specific should a character's world view be? Should how the character believes they can cast magick be more wave of the hand improvish (&quot;My character believes in Wicca, so in order to catch that guy, he's gonna light a candle and cause misfortune to befall him to make it easier to catch up.&quot;), or should it be more specific (&quot;My character believes in Wicca, so it wouldn't make sense for him to believe he's able to catch him.&quot;), or somewhere in between?<br /> 2. A character of Arete 9 or higher doesn't need to employ any instruments (ignoring the Technocrats), does this mean that they can perform any kind of Effect they want regardless of their worldview, or does it still need to fall within their beliefs of what magick is and how they perform it.<br /> 2b. If 2 is correct, does this mean Mages can slowly realize they can perform such magick that's slightly pushing outside their worldview, or is it a sudden &quot;A-ha!&quot; moment at Arete 9.<br /> <br /> If it's obvious I'm operating under a skewed and misunderstood knowing of how the magick system works, please correct me, because this has by far been the most nebulous part of learning M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28584,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28584-matter911","user":"Matter911","date":". 10-09-2024, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28584-matter911","name":"Matter911","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T02:39:29-07:00","id":1543504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matter911</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543429-m20-story-wise-questions-about-the-magick-system#post1543429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About to run my first M20 session, and while I understand how magick and casting Effects work mechanically, I do have some questions about casting magick, primarily with character's foci.<br /> <br /> 1. How specific should a character's world view be? Should how the character believes they can cast magick be more wave of the hand improvish (&quot;My character believes in Wicca, so in order to catch that guy, he's gonna light a candle and cause misfortune to befall him to make it easier to catch up.&quot;), or should it be more specific (&quot;My character believes in Wicca, so it wouldn't make sense for him to believe he's able to catch him.&quot;), or somewhere in between?<br /> 2. A character of Arete 9 or higher doesn't need to employ any instruments (ignoring the Technocrats), does this mean that they can perform any kind of Effect they want regardless of their worldview, or does it still need to fall within their beliefs of what magick is and how they perform it.<br /> 2b. If 2 is correct, does this mean Mages can slowly realize they can perform such magick that's slightly pushing outside their worldview, or is it a sudden &quot;A-ha!&quot; moment at Arete 9.<br /> <br /> If it's obvious I'm operating under a skewed and misunderstood knowing of how the magick system works, please correct me, because this has by far been the most nebulous part of learning M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - However specific, the character is by definition an experimenter, pushing the limits of their chosen system. Instead of thinking how specific it should be, just ask the player how they will fit the effect to their worldview, but don\u2019t use it to stop them from casting. Engaging with the question is what\u2019s important, there\u2019s no right answer.<br /> <br /> 2 - At this point the Mage realizes that they actually just impose their will upon the world. It most certainly doesn\u2019t have to fit a \u201chow you perform it\u201d because the point is precisely willing effects into existence without any instruments. In fact, the whole ditching Instruments aspect is about the Mage becoming more and more proficient at willing shit out of nothing. There\u2019s more nuance here, but that\u2019s the gist of it.<br /> <br /> 2b - Slowly realize.<br /> <br /> In Mage, always err on the side of letting players do things with Magic. As far as Magic goes, it is meant to let the PCs do as they please, like veritable gods. The point of the game isn\u2019t for the Magic to be balanced against something else, but to let PCs deal with their mistakes and the consequences of how they employ their considerable powers.<br /> <br /> Paradox, the Technocratic Union, or simply watch your loved ones devolve into mindless drones under the weight of too many Mind effects that seemed like a good idea in the past. Of course, there\u2019s nothing wrong with the consequences being good if their use of Magic is adequate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T03:29:59-07:00","id":1543507,"title":"","content":"1. At the very least he should know what he cant do (and i mean based on his paradigm not spheres mechanically)<br /> 2. At this stage the character is almost ready to let go of his paradigm<br /> 2b. its a slow process of evolving paradigm, it can go both described ways honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T11:03:06-07:00","id":1543532,"title":"","content":"I'm going to dissent a bit on #2 because it feels like the responses are a bit colored by older editions and don't take into account some of the changes M20 made.<br /> <br /> In M20, the overcoming of instruments doesn't inherently come with the older edition's idea of overall overcoming of Focus broadly (in Mage 1e - Revised things were handled differently such that everything in magical style came from paradigm). When you overcome your instruments, you can still use them for bonuses, so your character still believes in them on some level or that wouldn't make any sense. There's nothing in M20 that suggests that higher Arete leads to completely getting paradigm and practices, instead of expanded views of how to apply basic principles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T14:10:28-07:00","id":1543539,"title":"","content":"To expand on Heavy Arms's point, an Arete 9 Mage could easily be argued, internal to their Faction, to have exemplified their Paradigm. Someone so adept at their Art, they can go without their Instruments if they choose.<br /> <br /> The reasoning can be Paradigm-specific. The Celestial Chorus Archpriest has such a close relationship to the divine, they need not pray to know and do their divine will, or ask for intercession. The Hermetic Archmage has honed their Will into a knife's edge, the better to cut Reality into a shape of their choosing. A Solificati Archalchemist has transmuted their soul to True Gold, such that they, themselves, are the Philosopher's Stone.<br /> <br /> An Arete 9 character is not, by necessity, one who has transcended belief in their Focus. They may have, alternatively, &quot;got gud&quot; at their Focus.<br /> <br /> (This is also why Ascension isn't obtained simply by accruing magickal power. If anything, it's holding them back from transcending the world entirely. An exemplar who hews to their old understanding of the world - no matter how advanced or refined - will not Ascend.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}